    B: Be("In this story, what makes the customer unsure about his offer?", ["He cannot see the price card for his fruit.", "He has a basket but no money to offer.", "He has money but no fruit to buy.", "He cannot find any worker at the stall."], "Page 5: The customer holds fruit in one hand and money in the other. Without the price card, he cannot tell whether his offer is too much or too little."),
    C: Be("In this story, which missing information explains the customer’s hesitation?", ["The price card is missing, so he cannot judge the amount of his offer.", "He has not obtained any fruit, so he cannot compare two baskets.", "He has no money, so the worker must lend him a coin first.", "The worker is absent, so he cannot speak to anyone about a price."], "Page 5 does not describe a lack of fruit or money: he holds both. What he lacks is the price card needed to judge whether his offer is too much or too little.")
